  "scope": "Experimental ThresholdLean damage aggregation is applied only to the final step of each finite-horizon witness. Every such proof cell is separately enumerated with the native exact kernel and compared in four outcome categories: undecided, P1 win, P2 win, and tie. The archived tables, retained child mass, rational backups, fixed policies, controller queries, mixture and ceiling are independently checked. Numeric values and schedules equal those of the audited proof, with two runs per backend and zero/500ms controls. The equivalence is established only for the executed finite cells. A separate sandstorm counterexample proves that using this aggregation unconditionally at the horizon is unsound. Unchecked numeric results are therefore not general certificates. Timing excludes the native audit, loading and model replay. A sound runtime eligibility guard or exact outcome quotient is still required before adopting this beyond the audited experiment. No production integration or deployed-strength claim."
